.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt LONGBOAT 1
.Os Mavergreen
.Sh NAME
.Nm longboat
.Nd get an SDK, or install media, for a particular OS X
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm longboat
.Cm list
.Nm longboat
.Cm sdk list
.Nm longboat
.Cm sdk install
.Ar version
.Op Fl \-pkg\-only Ar DIR
.Nm longboat
.Cm sdk uninstall
.Ar version
.Nm longboat
.Cm sdk fetch
.Ar version
.Fl \-into Ar DIR
.Nm longboat
.Cm media list
.Nm longboat
.Cm media fetch
.Ar version
.Fl \-into Ar DIR
.Op Fl \-source\-recipe
.Op Fl \-source\-file Ar PATH
.Op Fl \-source\-url Ar URL Op Fl \-auth\-header\-env Ar NAME
.Op Fl \-source\-command Ar PATH
.Nm longboat
.Cm media verify
.Ar version
.Ar image
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
does two jobs, each for a particular OS X version such as 10.6, 10.9 or 11.3:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Cm sdk
puts that version's SDK on this machine, so a compiler can build against it, for example with
.Ql clang -isysroot /usr/local/mavergreen/sdk109/SDKs/MacOSX10.9.sdk .
.It
.Cm media
downloads that version's install media to this machine, held to its pins, for building a virtual
machine from.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
is an unofficial community tool, not affiliated with Apple.
SDKs are fetched from third-party mirrors onto your own machine and never redistributed.
.Pp
Each word has its own help:
.Dl longboat \-\-help | longboat sdk \-\-help | longboat media \-\-help
.Ql longboat \-\-help sdk
and
.Ql longboat \-\-help media
show the same as the word's own.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm Cm list
One line per OS X version either job knows: whether its SDK is
.Ql installed ,
.Ql available
or not offered
.Pq Ql \- ,
and whether its install media is
.Ql available
from a built-in recipe,
.Ql bring your own disc ,
or not known
.Pq Ql \- .
.It Nm Cm sdk list
One line per SDK version offered:
.Ar version short-name
.Cm installed | available .
.It Nm Cm sdk install Ar version Op Fl \-pkg\-only Ar DIR
Fetch the version's pinned SDK, check it against its SHA-256, build it into a package and install it.
Needs root and macOS.
Prints only the installed SDK's path on standard output, so
.Ql "$(sudo longboat sdk install 10.9)"
is that path.
With
.Fl \-pkg\-only Ar DIR ,
builds the package into
.Ar DIR
instead, without root, and prints its path.
.It Nm Cm sdk uninstall Ar version
Remove the installed SDK, with the
.Ic mavergreen
helper's
.Cm uninstall .
Needs root and macOS.
.It Nm Cm sdk fetch Ar version Fl \-into Ar DIR
Put the version's SDK in
.Ar DIR ,
checked against its SHA-256, without root and without installing it, and print its path.
A second run with the same
.Ar DIR
uses what is there.
.It Nm Cm media list
One line per version whose install media
.Nm
knows:
.Ar version
.Cm recipe | bring-your-own .
.It Nm Cm media fetch Ar version Fl \-into Ar DIR Op Ar sources
Put the version's install media in
.Ar DIR ,
as
.Pa InstallESD.dmg
(10.9) or
.Pa install-disc.img
(10.6), and print its path.
Nothing takes that name until it has passed the version's pins.
See
.Sx MEDIA SOURCES .
.It Nm Cm media verify Ar version Ar image
Hold an image you already have to the version's pins, and print
.Ar version build content-digest .
.El
.Sh MEDIA SOURCES
.Cm media fetch
tries its sources in the order given, keeps the first whose media passes the version's pins, and
accepts each flag more than once.
With no source flag it uses the built-in recipe.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-source\-recipe
The version's built-in recipe.
10.9's downloads
.Pa InstallESD.dmg
from Apple's servers.
10.6 has none: Apple does not serve it, so bring an image of a retail Snow Leopard DVD.
.It Fl \-source\-file Ar PATH
An image on this machine.
.It Fl \-source\-url Ar URL Op Fl \-auth\-header\-env Ar NAME
An image to download.
The request's header, written
.Ql Name: value ,
comes from the environment variable
.Ar NAME ,
never from the command line.
Neither the URL nor the header is ever printed.
.It Fl \-source\-command Ar PATH
A program on this machine, run with a stripped environment and given, as its last argument, a
directory to write exactly one image into.
.El
.Pp
Media is trusted by what it holds, never by where it came from: 10.9's
.Pa InstallESD.dmg
by its SHA-256, and a 10.6 disc by the SHA-256 of every package on it, so any faithful copy passes,
whatever made the image (an ISO, a Disk Utility .dmg or .cdr).
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar NAME
The variable
.Fl \-auth\-header\-env Ar NAME
names holds a download's
.Ql Name: value
header.
.It Ev TMPDIR
Where
.Cm sdk install
builds its package.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/mavergreen/sdk109/SDKs/MacOSX10.9.sdk
The 10.9 SDK, once installed; it exists exactly when
.Ql sdk109
is installed.
Each SDK has its own tree,
.Pa /usr/local/mavergreen/sdk Ns Ar NNN ,
its version without the dot; 11.3's is
.Pa /usr/local/mavergreen/sdk113/SDKs/MacOSX11.3.sdk .
.It Pa /usr/local/mavergreen/var/longboat
Where
.Cm sdk install
keeps the SDK downloads it has checked.
.It Pa /usr/local/mavergreen/longboat
.Nm
itself, on a Mac.
On Linux it runs from wherever its tarball is unpacked, under
.Pa opt/mavergreen/longboat .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
All is well.
.It 1
Refused or failed: media that does not pass its pins, a download that fails, an SDK that is not
installed, a broken installation of
.Nm .
.It 2
A usage error, an unknown version, a command that needs root or macOS run without it.
.El
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
On Linux,
.Cm list ,
.Cm sdk list ,
.Cm sdk fetch
and every
.Cm media
command work.
.Cm sdk fetch
needs
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr xz 1
and
.Xr shasum 1 .
.Cm sdk install
and
.Cm sdk uninstall
need macOS for now, and say so.
.Pp
Earlier releases spelled the commands differently.
These still work, after one line on standard error naming the new form:
.Bl -column "longboat verify installer" "longboat media verify" -offset indent
.It Sy Old Ta Sy Now
.It longboat install Ta longboat sdk install
.It longboat fetch Ar version Ta longboat sdk fetch
.It longboat fetch installer Ta longboat media fetch
.It longboat verify installer Ta longboat media verify
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clang 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/Mavergreen/longboat
